   "source": [
    "## Manual Insights (Written by the Analyst)\n",
    "\n",
    "<!-- MANUAL:START -->\n",
    "- **Structural missingness in `TotalCharges`:** Exactly 11 rows contain whitespace-only strings (`\" \"`) in `TotalCharges`, causing naive `pd.read_csv()` to misclassify the entire column as `object`. Every single one of those 11 customers has `tenure == 0` (newly signed up customers who have not yet been billed for their first month), meaning the missingness is structurally explained (**MAR** given `tenure == 0`), not random data corruption.\n",
    "- **Encoded binary demographic (`SeniorCitizen`):** Unlike `Partner` and `Dependents` (`Yes`/`No`), `SeniorCitizen` is encoded as `0`/`1` integers; our dataset config explicitly documents this as categorical/binary so it is treated consistently in group comparisons.\n",
    "- **Redundant category levels across add-on services:** Six service columns (`OnlineSecurity`, `OnlineBackup`, `DeviceProtection`, `TechSupport`, `StreamingTV`, `StreamingMovies`) share an identical `"No internet service"` level (21.6% of rows), which is perfectly collinear with `InternetService == \"No\"`. Phase 2/3 should note that chi-square tests across pairs of these add-on columns are driven primarily by the shared `"No internet service"` subgroup.\n",
    "- **Contract structure & early-tenure churn hazard:** Customers on `Month-to-month` contracts exhibit the highest churn rate (~42.7%), whereas `One year` (~11.3%) and `Two year` (~2.8%) contracts strongly retain subscribers. Churn is heavily concentrated in the first 1-6 months of `tenure`.\n",
    "- **Collinearity warning (`TotalCharges` vs `tenure x MonthlyCharges`):** `TotalCharges` is approximately the product `tenure * MonthlyCharges` (`r > 0.82` with `tenure`), so Phase 3/5 should expect opposite-direction univariate associations with `Churn` (`MonthlyCharges` positively associated with churn due to Fiber Optic pricing, while `TotalCharges` is negatively associated with churn because high `TotalCharges` requires long `tenure`).\n",
    "- **Reference findings for Phase 5 evaluation to recover:** (1) `Contract <-> Churn` (strong categorical association), (2) `tenure <-> Churn` (strong negative relationship), (3) `InternetService (Fiber optic) <-> Churn` (higher churn), (4) `OnlineSecurity / TechSupport <-> Churn` (protective effect), and (5) `PaymentMethod (Electronic check) <-> Churn`.\n",
    "<!-- MANUAL:END -->"
   ]
  }
